{"name":"Maiden Pink","hex":"#ff2feb","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"maiden","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A girl or an unmarried young woman.","A female virgin."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Virgin.","Without offspring."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/maiden"},{"term":"pink","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A color reminiscent of pinks, the flowers.","Magenta, the colour evoked by red and blue light when combined."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having a colour between red and white; pale red.","Of a fox-hunter's jacket: scarlet."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pink"}],"entries":[{"title":"Dianthus deltoides","blocks":[{"text":"Dianthus deltoides, the maiden pink, is a species of Dianthus native to most of Europe and western Asia. It can also be found in many parts of North America, where it is an introduced species."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c7/0_Dianthus_deltoides_alpinus_-_Yvoire.JPG/330px-0_Dianthus_deltoides_alpinus_-_Yvoire.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dianthus_deltoides"},{"title":"Virginity","blocks":[{"text":"Virginity is a social construct that denotes the state of a person who has never engaged in sexual intercourse. As it is not an objective term with an operational definition, social definitions of what constitutes virginity, or the lack thereof, vary. Heterosexual individuals may or may not consider loss of virginity to occur only through penile–vaginal penetration, while people of other sexual orientations often include oral sex, anal sex, or manual sex in their definitions of virginity loss. The term \"virgin\" encompasses a range of definitions, as found in traditional, modern, and ethical concepts. Religious rituals for regaining virginity exist in many cultures. Some men and women who practice celibacy after losing their virginity consider themselves born-again virgins."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1d/William-Adolphe_Bouguereau_%281825-1905%29_-Youth_%281893%29.jpg/330px-William-Adolphe_Bouguereau_%281825-1905%29_-Youth_%281893%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Virginity"},{"title":"Pink","blocks":[{"text":"Pink is a pale tint of red or rose, the color of the pink flower. It was first used as a color name in the late 17th century. A combination of pink and white is associated with innocence, whereas a combination of pink and black links to eroticism and seduction."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/Pink_sapphire_ring.jpg/330px-Pink_sapphire_ring.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pink"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9e/Chastity_%28a_virgin_and_a_unicorn%29._Oil_painting_by_a_followe_Wellcome_V0017113.jpg/500px-Chastity_%28a_virgin_and_a_unicorn%29._Oil_painting_by_a_followe_Wellcome_V0017113.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9e/Chastity_%28a_virgin_and_a_unicorn%29._Oil_painting_by_a_followe_Wellcome_V0017113.jpg/1280px-Chastity_%28a_virgin_and_a_unicorn%29._Oil_painting_by_a_followe_Wellcome_V0017113.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9e/Chastity_%28a_virgin_and_a_unicorn%29._Oil_painting_by_a_followe_Wellcome_V0017113.jpg/500px-Chastity_%28a_virgin_and_a_unicorn%29._Oil_painting_by_a_followe_Wellcome_V0017113.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A virgin and a unicorn, oil painting by an anonymous painter, ca. 1500","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AChastity_(a